{"type":"text","timestamp":1787347075260,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"id":"prt_0262fe876001BCdPkes5HMvrPk","messageID":"msg_0262f8871001bHvTq0Tmkdc0Mm","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","type":"text","text":"g2 passes. g3 crashes inside wasm3 — and I see why: `rt_realloc` returns the old block when the *size class* matches even when `n` exceeds that block's actual capacity → heap corruption. Fixing:","time":{"start":1787347069046,"end":1787347075244}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787347075260,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_6815d2b6df8e4fd595237586","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc","newString":"void *rt_realloc(void *p, uint64_t n) {\n    if (!p)\n        return rt_malloc(n);\n    hdr *h = (hdr *)p - 1;\n    uint64_t cap = h->size - sizeof(hdr);\n    if (!h->magic)\n        return p; /* foreign/raw block: cannot grow safely, leak-stable */\n    if (n <= cap)\n        return p; /* fits in existing capacity */\n    void *q = rt_malloc(n);\n    if (!q)\n        return 0;\n    uint64_t cp = cap < n ? cap : n;\n    uint8_t *dq = (uint8_t *)q, *sp = (uint8_t *)p;\n    for (uint64_t i = 0; i < cp; i++)\n        dq[i] = sp[i];\n    rt_free(p);\n    return q;\n}","oldString":"void *rt_realloc(void *p, uint64_t n) {\n    if (!p)\n        return rt_malloc(n);\n    hdr *h = (hdr *)p - 1;\n    uint64_t oldn = h->size - sizeof(hdr);\n    if (cls_of(((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL)) == cls_of(h->size))\n        return p;\n    void *q = rt_malloc(n);\n    if (!q)\n        return 0;\n    uint64_t cp = oldn < n ? oldn : n;\n    uint8_t *dq = (uint8_t *)q, *sp = (uint8_t *)p;\n    for (uint64_t i = 0; i < cp; i++)\n        dq[i] = sp[i];\n    rt_free(p);\n    return q;\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n===================================================================\n--- /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n+++ /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n@@ -66,15 +66,17 @@\n void *rt_realloc(void *p, uint64_t n) {\n     if (!p)\n         return rt_malloc(n);\n     hdr *h = (hdr *)p - 1;\n-    uint64_t oldn = h->size - sizeof(hdr);\n-    if (cls_of(((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL)) == cls_of(h->size))\n-        return p;\n+    uint64_t cap = h->size - sizeof(hdr);\n+    if (!h->magic)\n+        return p; /* foreign/raw block: cannot grow safely, leak-stable */\n+    if (n <= cap)\n+        return p; /* fits in existing capacity */\n     void *q = rt_malloc(n);\n     if (!q)\n         return 0;\n-    uint64_t cp = oldn < n ? oldn : n;\n+    uint64_t cp = cap < n ? cap : n;\n     uint8_t *dq = (uint8_t *)q, *sp = (uint8_t *)p;\n     for (uint64_t i = 0; i < cp; i++)\n         dq[i] = sp[i];\n     rt_free(p);\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc","patch":"Index: /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n===================================================================\n--- /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n+++ /home/cyr/kernel/core/rt.cc\n@@ -66,15 +66,17 @@\n void *rt_realloc(void *p, uint64_t n) {\n     if (!p)\n         return rt_malloc(n);\n     hdr *h = (hdr *)p - 1;\n-    uint64_t oldn = h->size - sizeof(hdr);\n-    if (cls_of(((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL)) == cls_of(h->size))\n-        return p;\n+    uint64_t cap = h->size - sizeof(hdr);\n+    if (!h->magic)\n+        return p; /* foreign/raw block: cannot grow safely, leak-stable */\n+    if (n <= cap)\n+        return p; /* fits in existing capacity */\n     void *q = rt_malloc(n);\n     if (!q)\n         return 0;\n-    uint64_t cp = oldn < n ? oldn : n;\n+    uint64_t cp = cap < n ? cap : n;\n     uint8_t *dq = (uint8_t *)q, *sp = (uint8_t *)p;\n     for (uint64_t i = 0; i < cp; i++)\n         dq[i] = sp[i];\n     rt_free(p);\n","additions":6,"deletions":4},"truncated":false},"title":"core/rt.cc","time":{"start":1787347075251,"end":1787347075256}},"id":"prt_026300085001c0rBTYNcKahMfY","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","messageID":"msg_0262f8871001bHvTq0Tmkdc0Mm"}}
