{"type":"text","timestamp":1787349936879,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"id":"prt_0265b7b7c001s6DVj3sf50HfvB","messageID":"msg_0265b0279001rzktn7EKTTKq9O","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","type":"text","text":"Reproduced on host — my allocator it is. Found the real bug: `cls_of` clamps oversize requests to the top class (512KB, not 8MB), silently returning undersized blocks, and `rt_free` then bins oversized blocks wrongly too. Fixing both:","time":{"start":1787349924732,"end":1787349936873}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787349937474,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_289f3eb2911a4f4b97f02f65","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='core/rt.cc'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''static int cls_of(uint64_t n) {\n    int c = 4;\n    while (((uint64_t)1 << c) < n) {\n        c++;\n        if (c >= NCLASS)\n            return NCLASS - 1;\n    }\n    return c;\n}'''\nnew='''/* smallest class c with 2^c >= n, or NCLASS when out of bands */\nstatic int cls_of(uint64_t n) {\n    int c = 4;\n    while (c < NCLASS && ((uint64_t)1 << c) < n)\n        c++;\n    return c;\n}'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\n\nold='''    uint64_t need = ((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL);\n    int c = cls_of(need);\n    /* Every block is rounded to its FULL class size so any pop from a\n     * bin always satisfies the request -- no capacity surprises. */\n    uint64_t clsz = (uint64_t)1 << c;\n    hdr *h;\n    if (bins[c]) {\n        h = bins[c];\n        bins[c] = h->next_free; /* size/magic stay intact */\n    } else {\n        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(clsz, 16);\n        if (!h)\n            return 0;\n        h->size = clsz;\n    }\n    h->magic = RT_MAGIC;\n    return (void *)(h + 1);'''\nnew='''    uint64_t need = ((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL);\n    int c = cls_of(need);\n    /* Every binned block is rounded to its FULL class size so any pop\n     * always satisfies the request -- no capacity surprises. */\n    hdr *h;\n    if (c < NCLASS) {\n        uint64_t clsz = (uint64_t)1 << c;\n        if (bins[c]) {\n            h = bins[c];\n            bins[c] = h->next_free; /* size/magic stay intact */\n        } else {\n            h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(clsz, 16);\n            if (!h)\n                return 0;\n            h->size = clsz;\n        }\n    } else {\n        /* oversized: exact allocation, never binned (leaked on free) */\n        h = (hdr *)mm_alloc(need, 16);\n        if (!h)\n            return 0;\n        h->size = need;\n    }\n    h->magic = RT_MAGIC;\n    return (void *)(h + 1);'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ng++ -std=c++20 -O1 -g -DNDEBUG -Icore -Iarch/x86_64 -Ithird_party/wasm3 -o /tmp/opencode/hosteng-rt tools/hosteng.cc /tmp/opencode/hoststubs.cc core/engine.cc core/sched.cc core/wasi_glue.cc core/rt.cc core/lib.cc /tmp/opencode/w3c/*.o 2>&1 | grep error | head -3; for g in 1 2 3; do timeout 60 /tmp/opencode/hosteng-rt build/hello$g.wasm </dev/null 2>&1 | grep -E 'hello|rc'; done","timeout":300000,"workdir":"/home/cyr/kernel"},"output":"ok\n[stage] spawned rc=0\nhello from C\n[sched] session exited rc=0x0\n[stage] spawned rc=0\nhello from Rust\n[sched] session exited rc=0x0\n[stage] spawned rc=0\nhello from Go\n[sched] session exited rc=0x0\n","metadata":{"output":"ok\n[stage] spawned rc=0\nhello from C\n[sched] session exited rc=0x0\n[stage] spawned rc=0\nhello from Rust\n[sched] session exited rc=0x0\n[stage] spawned rc=0\nhello from Go\n[sched] session exited rc=0x0\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='core/rt.cc'; s=open(p).read()\nold='''static int cls_of(uint64_t n) {\n    int c = 4;\n    while (((uint64_t)1 << c) < n) {\n        c++;\n        if (c >= NCLASS)\n            return NCLASS - 1;\n    }\n    return c;\n}'''\nnew='''/* smallest class c with 2^c >= n, or NCLASS when out of bands */\nstatic int cls_of(uint64_t n) {\n    int c = 4;\n    while (c < NCLASS && ((uint64_t)1 << c) < n)\n        c++;\n    return c;\n}'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new)\n\nold='''    uint64_t need = ((n + sizeof(hdr) + 15) & ~15ULL);\n    int c = cls_of(need);\n    /* Every block is rounded to its FULL class size so any pop from a\n     * bin always satisfies the request -- no capacity surprises. */\n    uint64_t clsz = (uint64_t)1 << c;\n    hdr *h;\n    if (bins[c]) {\n        h = bins[c];\n        bins[c] = h->next_free; /* size/magic stay intact */\n