{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787351027516,"sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_38f4ff3fccab4f0083d33731","state":{"status":"error","input":{"filePath":"/home/cyr/kernel/MEMORY.md","newString":"## Status (as of 2026-08-22)\n\n**Phase 3 gate GREEN (commit 39dc3fb).** wasm3 engine + frozen WASI\nprofile + session scheduler in kernel; guests hello.wat / hello.rs /\nhello.go all print via fd_write through the kernel (make test-all).\nToolchains: wat2wasm@~/.local/wabt, rustc wasm32v1-none target\n(RUSTUP_HOME=~/.local/rustup; wasip1 target's crt1 conflicts with\ncustom _start — use wasm32v1-none), stock go 1.24 GOOS=wasip1.\nNext: Phase 4 — port imports per ABI.md §1 + kernel-owned registry/\ndevman/power endpoints + console.wasm/login.wasm crash isolation.\n\nAllocator lessons (rt.cc, do not relearn):\n- free-list next ptr must NOT clobber hdr.size (separate field)\n- binned blocks are rounded to FULL class size so pops never undersize\n- cls_of returns NCLASS sentinel for oversized → exact alloc, leaked\n- host shim for rt.cc must use __libc_malloc aliases (std::malloc\n  resolves to your own definition = infinite recursion)\n- Go runtime imports fd_prestat_get at init and PANICS unless it gets\n  EBADF; poll_oneoff ENOSYS is fine for non-sleeping programs\n\nPhase-2 notes: C++ has no range designators (vm jump table fills at\nruntime); efi_main needs extern \"C\"; make test ~150s each (kernel\nhalts, QEMU eats 120s timeout) — budget bash timeouts accordingly.\n\nPhase-1 fixes: AllocatePool is 3-arg FW3 (was the loader regression);\nvasm pass-1 labels were all-zero (fixed); CPUID OSXSAVE reads 0 until\nCR4.OSXSAVE set; gate greps accept zero-padded hex.","oldString":"## Status (as of 2026-08-22)\n\n**Phase 2 gate GREEN (commit 1d92083).** core/ (C++20, arch-blind) +\narch/x86_64/ (uart cpu traps.S paging vector) split done; Plan 9 goshim\nreplaced by GNU as; gokernel/ deleted. Gate: TEST PASS from clean.\nNext: Phase 3 — vendor wasm3, mini-WASI profile, session scheduler,\nguest ladder C→Rust→Go. Phase-2 notes: C++ has no range designators\n(vm jump table fills at runtime); efi_main needs extern \"C\" or the\nlinker silently defaults the entry point; mm_alloc sits AFTER where\nmm_pool was in mm.cc (don't re-truncate it).\n\nPhase-1 fixes worth remembering:\n- loader regression was REAL: AllocatePool called via FW4 (extra\n  BootServices arg landed in Type slot → INVALID_PARAMETER). Now FW3.\n- vasm pass-1 bug: text labels all resolved to offset 0 (p.text fills in\n  pass 2) → every jz jumped to pc=0, guest spun silently forever. Host\n  harness for vm.c (/tmp pattern: stub serial/mm_alloc) is the fast way\n  to debug guest programs — use it before QEMU.\n- CPUID OSXSAVE bit27 reads 0 until CR4.OSXSAVE set; never gate on it.\n- Gate grep must accept zero-padded hex ('out 0x0000000000000028').\n- make test costs ~150s (kernel halts → QEMU runs to 120s timeout);\n  budget timeouts accordingly."},"error":"Could not find oldString in the file. It must match exactly, including whitespace, indentation, and line endings.","time":{"start":1787351027500,"end":1787351027512}},"id":"prt_0266c4f25001syhq7CoTj2td05","sessionID":"ses_fda1daed3ffeZ76o2z0rrfeMgg","messageID":"msg_0266bf675001RGqG2yqQeeEXGK"}}
